{
  "about": "What a Cell wears over its character, as data every screen draws from. Each theme holds pieces; a piece fills one slot, `wrap` round the body, `face` over it (never inside the eyes' boxes of cell.json) or `head` on top, and slots draw back to front in `slots`' order. `at` is a piece's top-left pixel from the body's top-left; a piece may rise above the body or reach past its sides. `art` is one string per row of pixels from the top, one letter per pixel, `.` clear, each letter an ink in `inks`, the same in every skin. A theme with no `season` is an outfit: the one the person picks in Settings › General › Outfit theme is worn, the `house` theme when none is picked. A theme with a `season` is worn over it while Seasons is on, from its `from` to its `to` (month-day, both days in, a window may run over the new year), the narrowest when two hold the day. A Cell wears one piece of each theme worn, dealt by its codename over the roster: each piece scores the words `codename|theme|piece`, ties to the first by name, and the Cells, first-born first, each take their highest-scoring piece among those held least, and keep it while they stay awake; a season's piece wins a slot both fill. Pieces hold still.",
